s are ceded.","m":12,"cp":"spanish-empire","cpn":"Spanish Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War","c":3},{"y":1898,"t":"gain","x":"10 December 1898: Spain cedes Puerto Rico, Guam and the Philippines.","m":12,"cp":"spanish-empire","cpn":"Spanish Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War","c":3},{"y":1898,"t":"occupation_end","x":"10 December 1898: the Treaty of Paris, 'signed by Spain and the United States on December 10, 1898' (in force 11 April 1899): 'Spain relinquished all claims of sovereignty over and title to Cuba.'","m":12,"cp":"spanish-empire","cpn":"Spanish Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1898)","c":3},{"y":1898,"t":"occupation_start","x":"10 December 1898: the occupation continues, now of land whose sovereignty Spain has given up, until independence on 20 May 1902 (below).","m":12,"cp":"republic-of-cuba","cpn":"Republic of Cuba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1898)","c":2},{"y":1899,"t":"gain","x":"17 January 1899: 'Wake Island was claimed.'","m":1,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":3},{"y":1899,"t":"contest_start","x":"4 February 1899: the Philippine-American War begins.","m":2,"cp":"first-philippine-republic","cpn":"First Philippine Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine%E2%80%93American_War","c":3},{"y":1900,"t":"gain","x":"16 February 1900: American Samoa.","m":2,"cp":"kingdom-of-samoa","cpn":"Kingdom of Samoa","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":3},{"y":1901,"t":"contest_end","x":"19 April 1901: the First Philippine Republic ends.","m":4,"cp":"first-philippine-republic","cpn":"First Philippine Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":3},{"y":1902,"t":"occupation_end","x":"20 May 1902: the US military government ends and Cuba becomes independent.","m":5,"cp":"republic-of-cuba","cpn":"Republic of Cuba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War","c":3},{"y":1903,"t":"gain","x":"20 October 1903: the Alaska boundary award.","m":10,"cp":"british-colonial-empire","cpn":"British Colonial Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":2},{"y":1903,"t":"gain","x":"10 December 1903: Guantanamo Bay is leased for a naval base.","m":12,"cp":"republic-of-cuba","cpn":"Republic of Cuba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":2},{"y":1904,"t":"gain","x":"19 May 1904: the Canal Zone.","m":5,"cp":"republic-of-panama","cpn":"Republic of Panama","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":3},{"y":1906,"t":"occupation_start","x":"September 1906: the second US occupation of Cuba.","m":9,"cp":"republic-of-cuba","cpn":"Republic of Cuba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1909,"t":"occupation_end","x":"23 January 1909: the US forces leave Cuba.","m":1,"cp":"republic-of-cuba","cpn":"Republic of Cuba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1915,"t":"occupation_start","x":"28 July 1915: the United States occupies Haiti.","m":7,"cp":"republic-of-haiti","cpn":"Republic of Haiti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1916,"t":"occupation_start","x":"May 1916: the United States occupies the Dominican Republic.","m":5,"cp":"dominican-republic","cpn":"Dominican Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1917,"t":"gain","x":"31 March 1917: the Virgin Islands.","m":3,"cp":"denmark-norway","cpn":"Denmark-Norway","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_United_States","c":3},{"y":1918,"t":"occupation_start","x":"December 1918: the Allied occupation of the Rhineland begins ('from 1 December 1918 until 30 June 1930'; the British entered on 1 December).","m":12,"cp":"german-empire","cpn":"German Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occupation_of_the_Rhineland","c":2},{"y":1923,"t":"occupation_end","x":"January 1923: 'the last Americans left their headquarters in Koblenz in January 1923' (the French were the last to leave, on 30 June 1930).","m":1,"cp":"german-empire","cpn":"German Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occupation_of_the_Rhineland","c":3},{"y":1924,"t":"occupation_end","x":"September 1924: the occupation of the Dominican Republic ends.","m":9,"cp":"dominican-republic","cpn":"Dominican Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1934,"t":"occupation_end","x":"15 August 1934: the occupation of Haiti ends.","m":8,"cp":"republic-of-haiti","cpn":"Republic of Haiti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1941,"t":"vassal_start","x":"April 1941: the United States takes Greenland under its protection Cliopatria draws 8,186 cells (2.1 M km2) of Greenland as plain US land from 1941 to 1945.","m":4,"cp":"greenland","cpn":"Greenland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1941,"t":"vassal_start","x":"7 July 1941: the United States takes over the protection of Iceland, 'by agreement with Iceland'.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-iceland","cpn":"Kingdom of Iceland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allied_occupation_of_Iceland","c":3},{"y":1941,"t":"occupation_start","x":"10 December 1941: Japan takes Guam.","m":12,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guam_(1941)","c":3},{"y":1941,"t":"occupation_start","x":"23 December 1941: Japan takes Wake.","m":12,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wake_Island","c":3},{"y":1942,"t":"occupation_start","x":"May 1942: Japan occupies the Philippines.","m":5,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines_campaign_(1941%E2%80%931942)","c":3},{"y":1942,"t":"occupation_start","x":"6 June 1942: Japan lands on Kiska.","m":6,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleutian_Islands_campaign","c":3},{"y":1942,"t":"occupation_start","x":"7 June 1942: Japan lands on Attu (see the Kiska event). empire-of-japan records the same occupation.","m":6,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleutian_Islands_campaign","c":3},{"y":1943,"t":"occupation_end","x":"29 May 1943: the United States retakes Attu.","m":5,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleutian_Islands_campaign","c":3},{"y":1943,"t":"occupation_end","x":"29 July 1943: Japan leaves Kiska.","m":7,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleutian_Islands_campaign","c":2},{"y":1944,"t":"occupation_end","x":"10 August 1944: the United States retakes Guam.","m":8,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guam_(1944)","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1945: the American zone of Austria.","cp":"second-republic-of-austria","cpn":"Second Republic of Austria","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":2},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1945: the occupation of Japan begins.","cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1945: the wartime protection of Iceland ends.","cp":"kingdom-of-iceland","cpn":"Kingdom of Iceland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allied_occupation_of_Iceland","c":2},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1945: the Amami Islands are under the same US administration (the start year is the researcher's reading of the Ryukyu administration of 22 June 1945). empire-of-japan records it.","cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Civil_Administration_of_the_Ryukyu_Islands","c":2},{"y":1945,"t":"vassal_end","x":"5 May 1945: the wartime protection of Greenland ends.","m":5,"cp":"greenland","cpn":"Greenland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland_in_World_War_II","c":2},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"5 June 1945: the Allied occupation of Germany begins 'from the Berlin Declaration on 5 June 1945' (Germany had 'formally surrendered' on 8 May 1945).","m":6,"cp":"nazi-germany","cpn":"Nazi Germany","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allied-occupied_Germany","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"22 June 1945: the US military administration of the Ryukyu Islands begins. empire-of-japan records the same occupation.","m":6,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Civil_Administration_of_the_Ryukyu_Islands","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_end","x":"2 September 1945: the last large Japanese force in the Philippines surrenders.","m":9,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomoyuki_Yamashita","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_start","x":"9 September 1945: the United States Army Military Government in Korea begins; it 'was the official ruling body of the southern half of the Korean Peninsula from 9 September 1945 to 15 August 1948'.","m":9,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Military_Government_in_Korea","c":3},{"y":1945,"t":"occupation_end","x":"4 September 1945: the Japanese garrison of Wake 'surrendered to a detachment of United States Marines on 4 September 1945'.","m":9,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wake_Island","c":3},{"y":1946,"t":"loss","x":"4 July 1946: the Philippines become independent.","m":7,"cp":"republic-of-the-philippines","cpn":"Republic of the Philippines","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States","c":3},{"y":1948,"t":"occupation_end","x":"15 August 1948: the military government hands over to the Republic of Korea: 'its first government officially proclaimed the existence of the Republic of Korea on 15 August 1948'; 'American troops finally withdrew in 1949'.","m":8,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Military_Government_in_Korea","c":3},{"y":1949,"t":"occupation_end","x":"23 May 1949: the Federal Republic is established in the west and the American zone becomes its land.","m":5,"cp":"nazi-germany","cpn":"Nazi Germany","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allied-occupied_Germany","c":3},{"y":1952,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1952: the occupation of Japan ends.","cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1953,"t":"occupation_end","x":"25 December 1953: the Amami Islands return to Japan (reversion 'made effective 25 December 1953').","m":12,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Civil_Administration_of_the_Ryukyu_Islands","c":3},{"y":1955,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1955: the occupation of Austria ends.","cp":"second-republic-of-austria","cpn":"Second Republic of Austria","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations","c":3},{"y":1972,"t":"occupation_end","x":"15 May 1972: 'control of Okinawa was given back to Japan on 15 May 1972'.","m":5,"cp":"empire-of-japan","cpn":"Japan (Empire of Japan, 1868-1947)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Civil_Administration_of_the_Ryukyu_Islands","c":3},{"y":1979,"t":"loss","x":"1 October 1979: 'the Canal Zone ceased to exist on October 1, 1979' under the Torrijos-Carter Treaties (signed 7 September 1977).","m":10,"cp":"republic-of-panama","cpn":"Republic of Panama","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panama_Canal_Zone","c":3},{"y":2003,"t":"occupation_start","x":"April 2003: the occupation of Iraq.","m":4,"cp":"iraqi-republic","cpn":"Iraqi Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_War","c":3},{"y":2004,"t":"occupation_end","x":"28 June 2004: the CPA is dissolved and sovereignty returns to Iraq.","m":6,"cp":"iraqi-republic","cpn":"Iraqi Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_War","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"American Revolutionary War","from":1776,"to":1783,"outcome":"United States victory: Britain recognised independence and a boundary at the Mississippi in the Treaty of Paris, signed 3 September 1783 (effective 12 May 1784); the last British troops left New York on 25 November 1783.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_War"},{"name":"Northwest Indian War","from":1786,"to":1795,"outcome":"United States victory: the Treaty of Greenville (1795) obliged the Confederacy to cede southern and eastern Ohio; the British gave up Fort Lernoult and Fort Miami in 1796 under the Jay Treaty.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwest_Indian_War"},{"name":"War of 1812","from":1812,"to":1815,"outcome":"Inconclusive (infobox): the Treaty of Ghent, December 1814, ratified 17 February 1815, 'restored the pre-war territorial status quo'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_1812"},{"name":"First Seminole War","from":1817,"to":1819,"outcome":"Jackson's army entered Spanish Florida on 15 March 1818 (he 'gathered his forces at Fort Scott in March 1818') and the Spanish surrendered Fort Barrancas at Pensacola on 28 May 1818; the Adams-Onis Treaty, signed 22 February 1819, transferred East and West…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Seminole_War"},{"name":"Mexican-American War","from":1846,"to":1848,"outcome":"United States victory: Mexico 'accepted the Rio Grande as its northern border' and ceded Alta California and Santa Fe de Nuevo Mexico for $15 million (Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo; effective 30 May 1848 on the Territory page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican%E2%80%93American_War"},{"name":"American Civil War","from":1861,"to":1865,"outcome":"United States victory: Lee surrendered at Appomattox on 9 April 1865; the Confederate cabinet dissolved on 5 May 1865; West Virginia was admitted on 20 June 1863 out of Virginia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War"},{"name":"Spanish-American War","from":1898,"to":1898,"outcome":"United States victory: protocol of peace 12 August, Treaty of Paris signed 10 December 1898 (in force 11 April 1899); Puerto Rico, Guam and the Philippines ceded for $20 million; Spain relinquished Cuba, occupied until 20 May 1902.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War"},{"name":"Philippine-American War","from":1899,"to":1902,"outcome":"United States victory: fighting began on 4 February 1899 in the Battle of Manila; Aguinaldo was captured on 23 March 1901 (oath of allegiance 19 April 1901, ending the First Philippine Republic); the war was officially declared over by the US on 4 July 1902.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine%E2%80%93American_War"},{"name":"World War I","from":1917,"to":1918,"outcome":"'On April 6, 1917, the United States declared war against Germany' (Timeline page entry '1917-1918').","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations"},{"name":"World War II","from":1941,"to":1945,"outcome":"On 8 December 1941 'the United States declared war against Japan'; Japan occupied Guam (10 December 1941), Wake (23 December 1941), the Philippines (May 1942), Kiska and Attu (June 1942); the United States retook Attu (29 May 1943), Guam (10 August 1944), the…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations"},{"name":"Korean War","from":1950,"to":1953,"outcome":"'The United States responded to the North Korean invasion of South Korea by going to its assistance' (Timeline page entry '1950-1953').","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations"},{"name":"Vietnam War","from":1955,"to":1975,"outcome":"The Timeline page lists '1955-1975: Vietnam War: U.S. military advisers had been in South Vietnam for a decade' as military involvement, not occupation, and the page ends in 1975.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_United_States_military_operations"},{"name":"Iraq War","from":2003,"to":2011,"outcome":"The invasion began on 20 March 2003; Baghdad fell on 9 April; the Coalition Provisional Authority ruled from 21 April 2003 to 28 June 2004, when it 'formally transferred sovereignty'; US forces were withdrawn on 18 December 2011.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_War"}],"certainty":[{"from":1776,"to":1782,"level":"soft","note":"A war with no agreed boundary: the British-held coast and the western posts moved with the campaigns."},{"from":1783,"to":1818,"level":"soft","note":"The Treaty of Paris lines are written (Mississippi, 31st parallel) but the northern line was unsurveyed, Spain held the Natchez strip until 1796, the British forts until 1796, the Maine boundary was disputed, and the Louisiana limits with…"},{"from":1819,"to":1860,"level":"sharp","note":"Treaty lines: the 49th parallel (1818), the Adams-Onis line (in force 1821), Webster-Ashburton (1842), the Oregon Treaty (1846), the Rio Grande and the cession (1848), Gadsden (1854)."},{"from":1861,"to":1865,"level":"soft","note":"The Civil War front moved campaign by campaign; the border-state lines and Confederate Arizona were never fixed."},{"from":1866,"to":1902,"level":"sharp","note":"Treaty and territorial lines; t